Package: opentelemetry-injector
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Provides:
 opentelemetry-injector1,
Description: OpenTelemetry LD_PRELOAD-based automatic instrumentation injector
 Installs libotelinject.so, a shared library loaded into every process via
 /etc/ld.so.preload.
 At runtime the library inspects each process to determine if it is a Java,
 Node.js, or .NET application and, if so, activates the corresponding
 auto-instrumentation agent whose path is configured in the conf.d/ drop-in
 files under /etc/opentelemetry/injector/conf.d/.
 .
 This package provides generation 1 of the injector configuration API
 (opentelemetry-injector1).
 If a future release breaks the conf.d contract it will provide
 opentelemetry-injector2 instead, and the package manager will block
 incompatible upgrades automatically.

Package: opentelemetry-java-autoinstrumentation
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Provides:
 opentelemetry-java-autoinstrumentation1,
Suggests:
 opentelemetry-injector1,
 default-jre,
Conflicts:
 opentelemetry-java-autoinstrumentation1,
Replaces:
 opentelemetry-java-autoinstrumentation1,
Description: OpenTelemetry Java Auto-Instrumentation Agent
 Packages the pre-built OpenTelemetry Java agent JAR from the upstream
 opentelemetry-java-instrumentation project.
 The JAR is installed at /usr/lib/opentelemetry/java/opentelemetry-javaagent.jar
 and a conf.d drop-in file is installed so that the opentelemetry-injector
 can activate it automatically for Java processes.
 .
 No files are downloaded at package installation time.

Package: opentelemetry-nodejs-autoinstrumentation
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 nodejs (>= 18),
Provides:
 opentelemetry-nodejs-autoinstrumentation1,
Suggests:
 opentelemetry-injector1,
Conflicts:
 opentelemetry-nodejs-autoinstrumentation1,
Replaces:
 opentelemetry-nodejs-autoinstrumentation1,
Description: OpenTelemetry Node.js Auto-Instrumentation
 Packages the pre-built @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node npm bundle
 from the upstream opentelemetry-js project.
 The node_modules tree is installed at /usr/lib/opentelemetry/nodejs/ and a
 conf.d drop-in file is installed so that the opentelemetry-injector can
 activate it automatically for Node.js processes.
 .
 No files are downloaded at package installation time.

Package: opentelemetry-dotnet-autoinstrumentation
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Provides:
 opentelemetry-dotnet-autoinstrumentation1,
Suggests:
 opentelemetry-injector1,
Conflicts:
 opentelemetry-dotnet-autoinstrumentation1,
Replaces:
 opentelemetry-dotnet-autoinstrumentation1,
Description: OpenTelemetry .NET Automatic Instrumentation
 Packages the pre-built OpenTelemetry .NET Automatic Instrumentation binaries
 for both glibc and musl libc flavours.
 The shared managed assemblies are installed once under
 /usr/lib/opentelemetry/dotnet/ and the native profiler library
 (OpenTelemetry.AutoInstrumentation.Native.so) is provided in both
 linux-x64/ (glibc) and linux-musl-x64/ (musl) subdirectories.
 .
 No files are downloaded at package installation time.

Package: opentelemetry
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 opentelemetry-injector1,
Recommends:
 opentelemetry-java-autoinstrumentation1,
 opentelemetry-nodejs-autoinstrumentation1,
 opentelemetry-dotnet-autoinstrumentation1,
Description: OpenTelemetry Auto-Instrumentation Suite (metapackage)
 A metapackage that installs the complete OpenTelemetry auto-instrumentation
 suite for Linux hosts: the LD_PRELOAD injector and language agents for Java,
 Node.js, and .NET.
 .
 Installing this package with:
   apt install opentelemetry
 is the recommended way to enable full auto-instrumentation on a host.
 .
 The injector is a hard dependency (Depends) because the metapackage is
 useless without it.
 Language agents are Recommends so that a user who does not need a specific
 language can remove it without tearing out the metapackage or leaving the
 remaining agents unprotected from autoremove.
